          "settings": {
            "question": "I’m on a GLP-1 treatment. Should I check with my doctor first?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Any supplement taken alongside a prescription should be discussed with the doctor who prescribed it — they know your treatment, your bloodwork and your history, and we don’t. Show them the ingredient list and let them tell you. That conversation comes first.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-2": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does GOMU replace my treatment?",
            "answer": "<p>No — and that isn’t its job. GOMU is a food supplement. It doesn’t treat, prevent or cure anything, and it has nothing to do with how your prescription works. What it does is cover daily nutritional intake — vitamins, key minerals, adaptogens, prebiotic fiber — for someone eating a lot less than they used to. Never change or stop a prescription on your own.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "When do I take it?",
            "answer": "<p>Whenever it fits your day. One pack, 8 gummies, chewed — with food or without, morning or afternoon. Nothing to measure, no water needed. The best time is the one you’ll actually keep.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much sugar is in it?",
            "answer": "<p>About 2g per pack — the minimum the gummy format requires. No added sugar beyond that, no artificial sweeteners. The exact figures are printed on every pouch.</p>"
          }
        },
